{# The colours, spacings and radii the whole interface is made of.

   Before this there were about sixty hard coded hex values across nine files
   and not one variable. `.card` existed in five copies with two different
   paddings, `.pill` in four with two incompatible designs, `table.aps` twice
   byte for byte, and `.stale` was amber on the start page and grey everywhere
   else — the same class name meaning two different things depending on which
   page you were looking at.

   One definition each, here, and every page that needs a colour asks for it by
   what it means rather than by what it looks like. #}
<style>
:root {
	/* ink */
	--ink: #222;
	--ink-soft: #445;
	--ink-mute: #667;
	--ink-faint: #889;

	/* surfaces and lines */
	--bg: #fff;
	--bg-soft: #f7f9fc;
	--bg-sunken: #f4f4f6;
	--line: #dde;
	--line-soft: #eee;
	--line-strong: #ccc;

	/* the three verdicts. Each has an ink, a background and a border, so a
	   pill, a tag and a bare word can all say the same thing. */
	--good: #2f6b33;
	--good-bg: #e8f5e9;
	--good-line: #b8ddb9;
	--bad: #900;
	--bad-bg: #fdecea;
	--bad-line: #f0b7b2;
	--warn: #8a5a10;
	--warn-bg: #fff4e5;
	--warn-line: #f0d3a8;
	/* a warning that has to be read at a glance in a table of numbers */
	--warn-strong: #b36b00;

	/* the accent, which is also the navigation */
	--accent: #24478f;
	--accent-bg: #e8f0fe;
	--accent-line: #b6ccf5;
	--nav-bg: #23303f;
	--nav-ink: #dfe6ee;
	--nav-hover: #35455a;
	--nav-active: #43587a;

	/* a source or provenance marker: neither good nor bad, just from elsewhere */
	--src: #5b4f86;
	--src-bg: #f3f0fa;
	--src-line: #dcd6ea;

	/* bars */
	--bar-bg: #e6e6ea;
	--bar-good: #4a8;
	--bar-weak: #d90;
	--bar-bad: #c33;
	--bar-plain: #7aa7d8;

	/* shape and rhythm */
	--r-sm: 3px;
	--r-md: 4px;
	--r-pill: 10px;
	--pad-card: .5rem .75rem;
	--fs-small: 85%;
	--fs-tiny: .72em;

	--mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
}
</style>
